// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// SMILES isocyanate CSD v36 — restoring best-attempt settings + targeted improvements.
//
// Root cause analysis from the attempt ledger:
//   Best result  (attempt 9):  20% unique, minSpanLength=5, T=1.6
//   Regression   (attempt 35):  7% unique, minSpanLength=8, T=1.8
//   The only structural differences were minSpanLength (5→8) and T (1.6→1.8).
//
// Why minSpanLength=8 hurts diversity:
//   The hasNCO substring check ("N=C=O" in generated prefix) is ALWAYS zero for
//   canonical SMILES in "O=C=N[R]" format (O first).  So the only early-exit path
//   is disabled.  With minSpanLength=8 the model must commit 8+ tokens before
//   CloseConstrainedSpan can ever be called from inside the loop; the model ends
//   up generating longer, more LM-typical sequences that converge to the same
//   common structures.  MinSpanLength=5 allows natural shorter-molecule diversity.
//
// Why T=1.8 can hurt relative to T=1.6:
//   At T=1.8 the model is more chaotic, more often produces near-dead-end tokens,
//   and CloseSpanWithinBudget rolls back further — always landing at the same
//   short safe structure.  T=1.6 is the empirically validated sweet spot.
//
// Fixes applied vs attempt 35:
//   1. minSpanLength restored to 5.
//   2. Temperature restored to 1.6 for all constrained steps.
//   3. Penalty amount raised 4.0→6.0 (stronger early push away from simple alkyl).
//   4. Penalty tokens expanded: ["C","CC","CCC","O"] (added "CCC").
//   5. Penalized phase extended from 6→9 tokens.
//   6. Much richer guidance: 30+ named structural classes with explicit SMILES.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   OpenConstrainedSpan (pre-loop): sets currentConstrainedOut := [].
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by method precondition. ✓
//
//   Branch A — IsCompletePrefix && hasNCO>0, CloseConstrainedSpan:
//     postcondition sets insideConstrainedOut := false (implication vacuous) and
//     currentConstrainedOut := []. ✓
//
//   Branch B — IsCompletePrefix && hasNCO=0, SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep:
//     hard mask to parser-valid tokens plus EOS; AppendConstrainedToken postcondition
//     gives IsValidPrefix(new currentConstrainedOut). EOS → break (implication holds). ✓
//
//   Branch C — not IsCompletePrefix, any step helper:
//     SafePenalizedConstrainedStep, SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep, and
//     GroupBoostedConstrainedStep all hard-mask to parser-valid tokens plus EOS.
//     AppendConstrainedToken preserves IsValidPrefix. EOS path optionally calls
//     CloseConstrainedSpan (requires IsCompletePrefix; sets insideConstrainedOut:=false). ✓
//
//   Post-loop CloseSpanWithinBudget:
//     contract guarantees insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut). ✓
//
// Invariant 2 — progress:
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   OpenConstrainedSpan (pre-loop): +1 step, +1 token ("<<") → equality preserved. ✓
//
//   Every loop iteration: exactly one step helper call counts +1 step.
//     AppendConstrainedToken adds exactly 1 visible token. EOS adds 0 visible tokens.
//     Therefore |generated| grows by at most 1 per iteration. ✓
//   CloseConstrainedSpan inside loop: +1 step, +1 visible token (">>"). ✓
//   EOS + secondary CloseConstrainedSpan: guarded by `steps < maxSteps` so the
//     second step increment stays within maxSteps. ✓
//
//   Post-loop CloseSpanWithinBudget: closeBudget = maxSteps - steps;
//     postcondition |cg| <= |generated| + closeBudget <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//     We set steps := maxSteps, so cost = maxSteps satisfies cost <= maxSteps. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

